<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Education on LebenInsider</title><link>https://lebeninsider.com/en/tags/education/</link><description>Recent content in Education on LebenInsider</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 11 Apr 2026 08:00:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://lebeninsider.com/en/tags/education/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Primary School: Turkey vs Germany</title><link>https://lebeninsider.com/en/germany/living/primary-school-turkey-vs-germany/</link><pubDate>Sat, 11 Apr 2026 08:00:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://lebeninsider.com/en/germany/living/primary-school-turkey-vs-germany/</guid><description>&lt;h1 class="relative group"&gt;Primary School: Turkey vs Germany&#10; &lt;div id="primary-school-turkey-vs-germany" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;span&#10; class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;&#10; &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#primary-school-turkey-vs-germany" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;/span&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;No homework until age 10. I had to read that twice.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 class="relative group"&gt;🇹🇷 Turkey: Academic Pressure, Early&#10; &lt;div id="-turkey-academic-pressure-early" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;span&#10; class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;&#10; &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#-turkey-academic-pressure-early" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;/span&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Turkish primary education begins at age 6 and places significant emphasis on academic performance from early on. Homework, exams, and ranking become part of a child&amp;rsquo;s life quickly. The pressure to perform well — to secure a place in a good secondary school, then university — begins earlier than many parents would choose.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>